 "inference": [
  "Plates are REDSEC/Gauntlet (Granite) content: the granted item and the only known granter are Battle Royale assets, and the multiplayer spawn path applies armor only when SpawnWithArmor (default 0) or a per-player value is set.",
  "ArmorGrantSpawnPlate switches on a spawn plate grant inside the ArmorGrant perk (a new gate on 2.1.1.0); by itself it gives multiplayer soldiers no armor.",
  "579 and 238 are hit-material ids: 579 the armored chest (EA's against-armor multipliers), 238 its ceramic-upgrade replacement. They select grid multipliers, not the armor curve; the curve choice is native.",
  "Against a plate the new curves cost up to one extra shot at capacity 40 and up to two at 80 (no spill); DMR shots rise from 4 to 5 at 0-30 m (capacity 40). Unplated BTK is unchanged (health curves did not move)."
 ],
